# Append-only experiment logs: every branch adds a row at the bottom of the same
# table, so parallel writeup branches conflict on each other even though the rows
# never overlap. The union merge driver keeps both sides' added lines instead of
# raising a conflict.
#
# Trade-off: union also keeps both versions when two branches genuinely edit the
# SAME row, which shows up as a duplicated row rather than a conflict. Rows are
# historical entries and are not normally revised, so that case is rare; when it
# happens, delete the stale copy. Row order follows merge order, not date order,
# so re-sort by date if a batch of branches lands out of order.
docs/model-experiments.md merge=union
docs/agent-experiments.md merge=union
